# Scratchpad for the three GitHub API calls in .claude/hooks/run-curator.sh.
# Local only — this whole folder is gitignored, token included.
#
# Click "Send Request" above any block. `###` separates requests.
# Blanks marked ____ are the parts to work out; everything else is wiring.

@slug   = vp1620/carOBD-II-Marketplace
@owner  = vp1620
@token  = {{$dotenv GH_TOKEN}}

# Point this at a branch you KNOW has an open PR while testing the read,
# then at one that has none to check the empty case.
@branch = tooling/decision-curator


### auth check — want 200. 401 = token not resolving, 403 = missing scope
GET https://api.github.com/user
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### baseline — every open PR. This is what a BROKEN filter returns.
GET https://api.github.com/repos/{{slug}}/pulls?state=open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json


### TODO 1 — find the open PR for {{branch}}.  want: exactly 1 result
# If this returns the same count as the baseline above, the filter is being
# ignored rather than applied — that failure is silent, so check the count.
# @name findPR
GET https://api.github.com/repos/{{slug}}/pulls?head=____&state=open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json


### TODO 2 — the DEC-n counter: every decisions/* PR, ANY state.
# All states, or a closed PR's number gets reused. Mind per_page — the
# default is 30, so a naive count silently undercuts once you pass it.
GET https://api.github.com/repos/{{slug}}/pulls?state=all&per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json


### TODO 3a — UPDATE an existing PR's body.
# Chains off findPR above: pulls .number straight out of its response, which
# is the dependent-variable problem solved without any shell.
PATCH https://api.github.com/repos/{{slug}}/pulls/{{findPR.response.body.$[0].number}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "rewritten from REST Client"
}


### TODO 3b — CREATE a PR.  Run against a scratch branch first:
#     git push origin main:refs/heads/scratch/api-test
# Then clean up:  gh pr close <n> --delete-branch
# Send it TWICE — you get two PRs. That non-idempotency is exactly why
# TODO 1's existence check has to exist.
POST https://api.github.com/repos/{{slug}}/pulls
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "scratch: api test",
  "head": "scratch/api-test",
  "base": "main",
  "body": "delete me"
}
